From: Jacob Cook <jacobmcook1984@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: rk817-charger: bound the boot soc with the ocv table

The boot state of charge comes from the columb counter, but the gauge
re-derives its own count from an ocv model whenever the pack rests
(GG_STS.OCV_UPD), so the counter can boot far from the truth. A GKD
Pixel2 came back from four hours powered off reading 31% with the pack
at 4.27V open circuit, and an RG353M booted on the charger at 25% at
4.125V; both had saved close to 94% and ran at a third of their real
charge until a full charge reset them.

  boot: counter 544036 uAh, saved soc 94480, fcc 1730 mAh, battery 4269990 uV

The ocv table bounds the state of charge from the terminal voltage
however the count was reached. Under load that voltage sits below the
open circuit voltage, so the table is a floor: a counter a tenth of the
pack below it is wrong, and the saved soc is kept. Under charge the
table is a ceiling, so the saved soc is kept only if the counter fell a
tenth of the pack below it and the ceiling allows that saved value; a
pack that really drained reads low, the ceiling rejects the stale save,
and the counter stands.

Also log the raw OFF_CNT, documented as decaminutes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-5-fable
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
@@ -854,8 +854,8 @@
 {
 	struct rk808 *rk808 = charger->rk808;
 	u32 boot_charge_mah;
-	int ret, reg, tmp;
-	bool first_boot;
+	int ret, reg, tmp, off_cnt, bat_uv, boot_soc, table_soc;
+	bool first_boot, keep_saved;
 	u8 bulk_reg[4];
 
 	/*
@@ -912,18 +912,41 @@
 		regmap_bulk_read(rk808->regmap, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_Q_PRES_H3,
 				 bulk_reg, 4);
 		tmp = get_unaligned_be32(bulk_reg);
+		regmap_read(rk808->regmap, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_OFF_CNT, &off_cnt);
+		bat_uv = rk817_bat_voltage_uv(charger, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_BAT_VOL_H);
 		dev_info(charger->dev,
-			 "boot: counter %d uAh, saved soc %d, fcc %d mAh, battery %d uV\n",
+			 "boot: counter %d uAh, saved soc %d, fcc %d mAh, battery %d uV, off_cnt %d\n",
 			 tmp > 0 ? ADC_TO_CHARGE_UAH(tmp, charger->res_div) : 0,
-			 charger->soc, charger->fcc_mah,
-			 rk817_bat_voltage_uv(charger, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_BAT_VOL_H));
+			 charger->soc, charger->fcc_mah, bat_uv, off_cnt);
 		if (tmp > 0) {
 			boot_charge_mah = ADC_TO_CHARGE_UAH(tmp,
 							    charger->res_div) / 1000;
 			if (boot_charge_mah > charger->fcc_mah)
 				boot_charge_mah = charger->fcc_mah;
-			charger->soc = boot_charge_mah * 100000 /
-				       charger->fcc_mah;
+			boot_soc = boot_charge_mah * 100000 / charger->fcc_mah;
+
+			/*
+			 * The gauge re-derives this count from its own ocv
+			 * model while the pack rests, so bound it with the ocv
+			 * table: under load the terminal voltage sits below the
+			 * open circuit voltage, making the table a floor, and
+			 * under charge above it, making it a ceiling on any
+			 * saved soc that would displace the counter.
+			 */
+			table_soc = power_supply_batinfo_ocv2cap(bat_info, bat_uv,
+								 20) * 1000;
+			if (charger->plugged_in)
+				keep_saved = boot_soc < charger->soc - 10000 &&
+					     charger->soc <= table_soc + 10000;
+			else
+				keep_saved = boot_soc < table_soc - 10000;
+
+			if (keep_saved)
+				dev_info(charger->dev,
+					 "counter %d, voltage allows %d, keeping saved soc %d\n",
+					 boot_soc, table_soc, charger->soc);
+			else
+				charger->soc = boot_soc;
 		} else {
 			dev_info(charger->dev,
 				 "columb counter invalid, keeping saved soc\n");
